<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="pathbeaters26" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
  <metadata><name>Big Boulder Lakes via Walker Lake</name><desc>Trail legs from OpenStreetMap via BRouter; off-trail legs above Walker Lake are terrain-fitted least-cost lines on a 40 m elevation grid, not surveyed tracks. Follow cairns and the map; treat these as guidance.</desc></metadata>
  <wpt lat="44.131137" lon="-114.513280"><ele>2186</ele><name>Trailhead · Big Boulder Creek at Livingston Mill</name><desc>Sign the register. Dispersed car camping at the road end if the weather stops the Thursday hike-in.</desc><sym>Trail Head</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.111142" lon="-114.575389"><ele>2629</ele><name>Thu camp · Big Boulder Creek bench (~4 mi, approx.)</name><desc>Thursday hike-in camp if the weather holds: forested bench near the creek just past the Frog Lake junction. Position from the routed track, not a surveyed site.</desc><sym>Campground</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.106600" lon="-114.601800"><ele>2836</ele><name>Walker Lake, west end · start of the use trail</name><desc>Trail 601 ends here. Cairned use trail climbs north-west up the open rocky slope to the pass above Hook Lake. Alternative camp: Walker Lake (fires legal).</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.104576" lon="-114.607973"><ele>3025</ele><name>Pass above Hook Lake (approx.)</name><desc>High point of the use trail. On the way down, the route fades near the bottom and wanders toward the cliffs above Walker Lake: stay on this line.</desc><sym>Summit</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.104660" lon="-114.608060"><ele>3025</ele><name>Hook Lake</name><desc>Pass-through, no camps.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.101250" lon="-114.608330"><ele>3002</ele><name>Fri–Sun camp · Cove Lake</name><desc>Basin camp for three nights. Sites at the southeast corner and back from the water; stoves only above 8,800 ft. Rock spine above camp for the view.</desc><sym>Campground</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.102900" lon="-114.615000"><ele>3016</ele><name>Sapphire Lake · alt camp</name><desc>Established site at the outlet, peninsula site. Best fishing.</desc><sym>Campground</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.106500" lon="-114.620930"><ele>3067</ele><name>Cirque Lake</name><desc>Under the east face of D.O. Lee. Talus above it leads to the saddle for the peak.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.107500" lon="-114.625500"><ele>3212</ele><name>The Kettles (approx.)</name><desc>White shattered-rock moraine above Cirque Lake, ~10,300 ft.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.103500" lon="-114.625000"><ele>3174</ele><name>Ridge bench above Cirque (approx.)</name><desc>Overlook of the basin; start of the D.O. Lee scramble.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.098500" lon="-114.633000"><ele>3134</ele><name>D.O. Lee Peak (approx. position)</name><desc>11,342 ft. Class 3 via the saddle north of the peak; the downclimb is the crux.</desc><sym>Summit</sym></wpt>
  <trk><name>Big Boulder Lakes via Walker Lake</name>
